// Write elision across a release fence, remapped against po.
//
// x := 2 elides x := 1 (write elision), as nothing is ppo-between them: the
// fence orders x := 1 before y := 1, the acquire read orders r1 before x := 2,
// and y := 1 is ordered before r1 by location, but ppo is not transitive.
// Remapping ppo along the elision (sMRD's forwarding context) sends the elided
// x := 1 onto x := 2, so its fence edge becomes x := 2 -> y := 1, closing the
// ppo cycle x := 2 -> y := 1 -> r1 -> x := 2: the elaborations do not keep ppo
// acyclic, the no-thin-air axiom does, and rejects every execution using this
// elision.
//
// MoRDor used to elide x := 1 here too, and kept executions with the elision
// consistent: it dropped the elided event from the execution and ordered a
// release fence by edges into the fence rather than across it, so no cycle
// arose. Since #207 it does not elide a write across a release fence at all:
// sMRD keeps elided writes out of coherence, and a thread synchronising with
// the fence would happen after x := 1 but not after x := 2. The golden went
// from 16 executions to 5.
//
// The elision changes no outcome, the execution without it remains: r2 may
// still read 1.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  fence(rel);
  y := 1;
  r1 :acq= y;
  x := 2
} ||| {
  r2 := x
}
%%
allow (r2 = 1) [sMRD]
